Document parsing in DeepDocParse-Web is performed by the DeepDocParse service
layer, and is powered by MinerU
(https://github.com/opendatalab/MinerU).

MinerU adds terms on top of Apache-2.0. Section 2 requires that any product
providing an online service built on MinerU state clearly and prominently, in
the product UI or in public documentation, that it uses MinerU; section 3
terminates the license automatically -- without notice -- on violation.
DeepDocParse-Web is exactly such a service -- it is the user-facing product --
so this attribution appears in:

  - this NOTICE file
  - README.md, at the top of the page
  - the product UI, in a footer shown on every page (AppShell.vue)

